I had been having problems with getting messages like "Couldn't load
minefill.lev" and so forth; after emailing the bug mailing list, I found
out that NetHack didn't know where to look, so the NetHack.cnf file
had to be edited, such that the PATH line looked like:
	PATH=NetHack:;HackExe:
However, even after doing this I still had this problem.  After investigating
I realized that the problem was with the NewGame icon used by HackWB.
Tooltypes in this icon take precedence over any settings in the NetHack.cnf
file.  The PATH= tooltype still had the old path, so I edited it using
the WorkBench info requester.  (I don't edit the icon through HackWB because
every time I do, the CHARACTER= tooltype gets changed from
"CHARACTER=" to "CHARACTER=RANDOM" -- something I don't want.  I like to choose
my character class each time I play.  Besides, for some reason, when the
tooltype is "CHARACTER=RANDOM" it always picks Rogue.)

I would recommend therefore that anyone who uses HackWB edit the NewGame
icon in their NetHack: directory to fix the PATH= tooltype.

Hope this saves someone some aggravation!

